      {
        "id": 151190,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-12-04T17:50:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I found the chat kind of annoying in that it's in a separate sort of pop-up window thingy rather than being visible on-screen at all times. It makes discussing strategy kind of a pain, as mentioned above. I tend to ask people not to use that suggestion thingy for me at all because it's <span class=\"bbcode-i\">my</span> deck, so <span class=\"bbcode-i\">I</span> will decide what to play. If people want to suggest something in the <span class=\"bbcode-i\">chat</span> with reasons why, then fine. Having everyone's hands visible helps because then I can suggest stuff myself based on what I see them holding and we can set up some kind of cool combo or something. A voice chat would be very helpful, yeah :).</p>\n<p>I haven't actually played the Steam version for some time now, though I expect the bug that put me off doing so was fixed ages ago (the one where you get disconnected then treated like a lurker by the game when you get back in, so you can't play any of your cards). I will have to get back into it at some point.</p>",
